      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are three strong thesis statement options for your essay:\n\n1. The Electoral College maintains a system where two-party dominance and winner-take-all rules systematically disenfranchise voters in suburban and swing states, making it essential to replace it with a direct national popular vote to ensure every citizen's voice aligns with democratic principles.\n2. Because the current system incentivizes political machines over grassroots voter preference and allows states with small populations to wield disproportionate power, abolishing the Electoral College in favor of the popular vote would level the playing field and restore true equal representation.\n3. The fundamental flaws of the Electoral College, including itsstoning of popular vote outcomes in historical instances, prove it is misaligned with the concept of a unified democracy, thus justifying a complete transition to a nationwide ballot count for fairer results.",
